  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 102.07 Advanced recycling",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 102.07 “Advanced recycling” means “advanced recycling” as defined in RSA 149-M:4, I-a, namely “a manufacturing process for the conversion of post-use polymers and recovered feedstocks into basic raw materials, feedstock chemicals, and other products like waxes and lubricants through processes that include pyrolysis, gasification, depolymerization, catalytic cracking, reforming, hydrogenation, solvolysis, and other similar technologies. For the purposes of this chapter, the primary products of advanced recycling shall not include hydrocarbons which are marketed, sold, or used as fuel for energy. Incidental products may be used for fuel only within the facility. For the purposes of this chapter, \"advanced recycling\" shall not be considered solid waste management, solid waste processing, waste processing, treatment, incineration, or combustion.”\n\nSource. #14103, eff 10-23-24 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw100.html"
